# Generate SDKs and artifacts

From the project containing `trellis.toml`, run:

```sh
trellis update
trellis generate
```

The Orders project's output is one ordinary ESM package:

```text
trellis/
  package.json
  index.js
  index.d.ts
  apis/
  participants/
  artifacts/apis/
  artifacts/participants/
```

`trellis.toml` declares `format = 1` and `name = "orders-trellis"`. The generated
package version is always `0.0.0`; API releases and participant identities remain
independent. The runtime dependency matches the CLI version. Artifact JSON is
tooling material, including referenced APIs, not a language import surface.

A root `package.json`, `deno.json`, or `deno.jsonc` selects TypeScript/JavaScript;
`Cargo.toml` selects Rust. One language defaults to `trellis/`, optionally
overridden by `[generate].output`. A mixed project requires explicit destinations:

```toml
format = 1
name = "orders-trellis"

[generate.rust]
output = "crates/orders-trellis"

[generate.typescript]
output = "packages/orders-trellis"
```

Each destination is one cohesive ordinary package, with separate `apis` and
`participants` namespaces. There is no language-selection setting. An API-only
project without a supported language marker generates no package.

`trellis generate` is offline. Local dependencies compile from source; registry
dependencies use exact validated API values from the global OCI cache and
`trellis.lock`. Compilation and rendering retain canonical values in memory;
publication uses compiled owned APIs directly. Failed compilation or rendering
preserves last-good output, and generation protects unrelated user files.

In CI or a fresh checkout, `trellis install` reproduces locked dependency
APIs in the global cache and generates the language packages. No project-local
installation tree or persistent generation index is created. Use `trellis update` when you
intend to resolve dependency changes, not merely to rebuild an existing lock.

Commit the generated package, as this example does, when a clone must build and
test without the Trellis CLI or API cache. Consumers use ordinary package-manager
dependencies; generation never rewrites their language manifests.
